<title>UK: BT Q3 pretax profit rises to 909 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BT Q3 pretax profit rises to 909 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.4		    vs 8.7</p>
<p> Redundancy charges     39		     vs 60</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    909		    vs 829</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,763		  vs 3,620</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 860 and 920 million stg. Pretax profits were after a 39 million stg redundancy charge, these exceptional charges being included in operating profits.</p>
<p>Full company name is British Telecommunications Plc  </p>
<p>Nine months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		25.7		   vs 25.5</p>
<p> Exceptional charges    274		    vs 183</p>
<p> Pretax		     2,508		  vs 2,435</p>
<p> Turnover		   11,129		 vs 10,668</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
